      "why": "pipelined_m is the only family that can plausibly meet the 0.44us batch latency constraint while minimising area. With m=8, latency is ceil(N/8)+2 cycles. For N=12-16, latency is 3-4 cycles. At Fmax ~200-300 MHz, 4 cycles = 13-20ns, well under 440ns. The 32-request burst is handled by the pipeline accepting one request per cycle, so all 32 are in-flight within 32 cycles, and results stream out at 1/cycle. The batch p99 latency is dominated by the pipeline latency + queueing, which should be well within 0.44us. Area is minimised by keeping N and data_width low while meeting accuracy_bits >= 12. m=4-8 balances pipeline depth (area) against latency."
    }
